<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<tt xml:lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata" xmlns:tts="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#styling" xmlns:ttp="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#parameter" ttp:profile="http://www.w3.org/TR/profile/sdp-us" >
<head>
<styling>
<style xml:id="s1" tts:textAlign="center" tts:extent="90% 90%" tts:origin="5% 5%" tts:displayAlign="after"/>
<style xml:id="s2" tts:fontSize=".72c" tts:backgroundColor="black" tts:color="white"/>
</styling>
<layout>
<region xml:id="r1" style="s1"/>
</layout>
</head>
<body region="r1">
<div>
<p begin="00:00:05.200" end="00:00:08.500" style="s2">The CEO of Graytech is marrying into <br />one of those billionaire families.  </p>
<p begin="00:00:09.900" end="00:00:13.900" style="s2">I&#39;ve seen that watch on a magazine cover. <br />It costs a fortune. It&#39;s a pot of Phipe.</p>
<p begin="00:00:17.800" end="00:00:23.200" style="s2">Galen, what did you do? Why is the engagement <br />off? Keep this up and I&#39;ll put Nate in your place.  </p>
<p begin="00:00:23.200" end="00:00:27.400" style="s2">No one takes what&#39;s mine. How dare you <br />talk to me like that, you useless idiot.</p>
<p begin="00:00:38.900" end="00:00:42.900" style="s2">Excuse me. You dropped your <br />bread. I don&#39;t want it.  </p>
<p begin="00:00:44.300" end="00:00:52.800" style="s2">You mean you&#39;re throwing it away? That&#39;s right. <br />Would you mind if I had it? My boyfriend&#39;s  </p>
<p begin="00:00:52.800" end="00:01:01.600" style="s2">proposing to me. I spent all my money on a gift <br />for him. I found this lucky coin by the fountain  </p>
<p begin="00:01:01.600" end="00:01:08.500" style="s2">this morning. I&#39;d like you to have it. I <br />hope it brings you good luck. Thank you.</p>
<p begin="00:01:12.800" end="00:01:14.500" style="s2">Well, she&#39;s interesting.</p>
<p begin="00:01:19.500" end="00:01:25.800" style="s2">Simon, once we&#39;re married, I&#39;ll keep backing your <br />business, even if it takes everything I have.</p>
<p begin="00:01:38.700" end="00:01:44.500" style="s2">Mom, Dad, I got into the startup incubator. I <br />can finally launch my business in San Francisco.</p>
<p begin="00:01:49.000" end="00:01:53.800" style="s2">They&#39;re not giving you any government <br />funding. What&#39;s there to celebrate? I  </p>
<p begin="00:01:53.800" end="00:01:58.400" style="s2">don&#39;t have money to bankroll you. How are <br />we supposed to fund a business on what we  </p>
<p begin="00:01:58.400" end="00:02:03.993" style="s2">make doing odd jobs? Find yourself a rich <br />woman. Take some pressure off this family.  </p>
<p begin="00:02:04.893" end="00:02:11.593" style="s2">People like us starting businesses, that&#39;s money <br />down the drain. You might as well buy me a drink.</p>
<p begin="00:02:18.193" end="00:02:22.993" style="s2">Don&#39;t tear it up. You can&#39;t throw away <br />an opportunity like this. I&#39;ll help you.  </p>
<p begin="00:02:24.293" end="00:02:26.793" style="s2">You grew up in a children&#39;s <br />home. You just got into MIT  </p>
<p begin="00:02:26.793" end="00:02:29.793" style="s2">and you don&#39;t even know how you&#39;ll <br />pay tuition. How could you help me?  </p>
<p begin="00:02:30.793" end="00:02:34.793" style="s2">I&#39;ll work around my classes. I&#39;ll earn <br />enough to help you get your business started.</p>
<p begin="00:02:54.393" end="00:03:00.693" style="s2">Leela, I asked you here because I&#39;m breaking up <br />with you. You&#39;re breaking up with me? Last month,  </p>
<p begin="00:03:00.693" end="00:03:04.793" style="s2">you said business was picking up. <br />You said you were going to propose.</p>
<p begin="00:03:12.193" end="00:03:17.593" style="s2">My son&#39;s successful, young, and handsome. <br />Women are lining up for him. You&#39;re  </p>
<p begin="00:03:17.593" end="00:03:23.293" style="s2">a waitress at some club. You think you&#39;re <br />good enough for him? Have some selfrespect.</p>
<p begin="00:03:28.193" end="00:03:36.093" style="s2">You expect my son to propose and this cheap thing <br />is what you got him in return? Dream on. Simon,  </p>
<p begin="00:03:36.093" end="00:03:42.493" style="s2">say something. Giving him a little startup money <br />doesn&#39;t mean you get to cling to him forever.  </p>
<p begin="00:03:43.893" end="00:03:50.493" style="s2">You might as well know. My son already proposed <br />to the marketing manager at Greytech. Look what  </p>
<p begin="00:03:50.493" end="00:03:56.593" style="s2">she gave him in return. Take your cheap <br />crap and get lost, Laya. From now on,  </p>
<p begin="00:03:56.593" end="00:04:02.994" style="s2">we don&#39;t know each other. Too trusting <br />for your own good. That never ends well.  </p>
<p begin="00:04:03.994" end="00:04:08.094" style="s2">Consider this a thank you for the coin. <br />You&#39;re in for the surprise of your life.</p>
<p begin="00:04:14.194" end="00:04:19.394" style="s2">Apado Phipe. I&#39;ve seen that watch <br />in the store. It&#39;s worth millions.  </p>
<p begin="00:04:19.894" end="00:04:26.794" style="s2">What rich family did he come from? <br />What are you staring at? You think  </p>
<p begin="00:04:26.794" end="00:04:29.894" style="s2">a man like that would look twice <br />at an ugly little nobody like you?</p>
<p begin="00:04:39.294" end="00:04:40.494" style="s2">I&#39;m here to ask you to marry me.</p>
<p begin="00:04:43.994" end="00:04:50.494" style="s2">Please don&#39;t make fun of me, sir. She&#39;s broke. <br />She scrapes by doing odd jobs. She&#39;s nowhere  </p>
<p begin="00:04:50.494" end="00:04:55.994" style="s2">near your league. She could work for a hundred <br />years and still not afford that watch of yours.</p>
<p begin="00:05:01.494" end="00:05:05.994" style="s2">I decide who&#39;s good enough for me. You <br />don&#39;t get a vote. That&#39;s the ring of  </p>
<p begin="00:05:05.994" end="00:05:09.894" style="s2">one of San Francisco&#39;s oldest families. That <br />ring will get you in anywhere in this city.</p>
<p begin="00:05:13.094" end="00:05:16.994" style="s2">I&#39;m asking you to marry me with this <br />ring. Do you believe I&#39;m serious now?  </p>
<p begin="00:05:17.594" end="00:05:24.894" style="s2">Sir, marriage isn&#39;t something you joke about. <br />Drop the act, Laya. Men from families like his  </p>
<p begin="00:05:24.894" end="00:05:29.794" style="s2">marry women from families like theirs. <br />Not some lowass waitress. You even got  </p>
<p begin="00:05:29.794" end="00:05:36.194" style="s2">a fake ring. It&#39;s pathetic. I didn&#39;t know <br />you had it in you. Paying someone to put  </p>
<p begin="00:05:36.194" end="00:05:42.694" style="s2">on this little show. You&#39;ve hit a new low, <br />Yla. Hiring a man to pretend he wants you.</p>
<p begin="00:05:47.594" end="00:05:54.894" style="s2">Play all the games you want, Laya. I&#39;m not <br />changing my mind. You have no place in my life.</p>
<p begin="00:06:02.794" end="00:06:08.895" style="s2">you. If you can&#39;t watch your mouth, I&#39;ll teach you <br />how. You&#39;re just some male assistant Laya hired  </p>
<p begin="00:06:08.896" end="00:06:15.496" style="s2">from a club. Who do you think you&#39;re fooling? <br />If this is real, go get married right now.</p>
<p begin="00:06:18.796" end="00:06:19.296" style="s2">Let&#39;s go.</p>
<p begin="00:06:26.396" end="00:06:27.396" style="s2">So,</p>
<p begin="00:06:27.396" end="00:06:31.496" style="s2">isn&#39;t this a little fact? I <br />don&#39;t waste time. [snorts]</p>
<p begin="00:06:37.096" end="00:06:40.496" style="s2">I&#39;ll sign. It&#39;s not like I <br />have anything left to lose.</p>
<p begin="00:06:47.996" end="00:06:48.996" style="s2">[snorts]</p>
<p begin="00:06:48.996" end="00:06:55.496" style="s2">They actually got married. Why would a handsome <br />young man like him marry that little [ __ ]  </p>
<p begin="00:06:56.096" end="00:06:58.796" style="s2">Leela is my wife now. Disrespect her again</p>
<p begin="00:07:02.696" end="00:07:04.096" style="s2">and you&#39;ll pay a price you can&#39;t afford.</p>
<p begin="00:07:20.296" end="00:07:25.096" style="s2">This room is bigger than my entire apartment. <br />Everything in here looks so expensive.  </p>
<p begin="00:07:25.096" end="00:07:32.396" style="s2">When I&#39;m not working, this is where I like to be. <br />Relax. Take a seat. Everything here is yours, too.  </p>
<p begin="00:07:34.596" end="00:07:36.396" style="s2">Sir, who exactly are you?</p>
<p begin="00:07:39.596" end="00:07:42.796" style="s2">Gale Gray. Why does that name sound so familiar?</p>
<p begin="00:07:46.896" end="00:07:50.596" style="s2">Graytech CEO Galen Gray signed a strategic <br />partnership agreement with the Silicon  </p>
<p begin="00:07:50.596" end="00:07:54.096" style="s2">Valley Research Institute today. Under his <br />leadership, Gray Techch&#39;s market value has  </p>
<p begin="00:07:54.096" end="00:07:59.696" style="s2">surpassed 10 billion. The CEO of Graytech <br />proposed to me and I actually married him.  </p>
<p begin="00:08:00.696" end="00:08:06.596" style="s2">I married into that kind of money. Well, am <br />I good enough for you? Please don&#39;t tease me.  </p>
<p begin="00:08:07.596" end="00:08:13.297" style="s2">Someone as important as you stepping in to help <br />me. I&#39;m already so grateful. I couldn&#39;t possibly  </p>
<p begin="00:08:13.297" end="00:08:19.497" style="s2">ask for more. I&#39;ll divorce you tomorrow. I <br />promise I won&#39;t get in your way. You a spy.  </p>
<p begin="00:08:19.497" end="00:08:23.897" style="s2">I stood up for you. And this is <br />how you repay me. Married today,  </p>
<p begin="00:08:23.897" end="00:08:29.397" style="s2">divorced tomorrow. What kind of man do you take <br />me for? Please. That&#39;s not what I meant. I just  </p>
<p begin="00:08:29.397" end="00:08:34.897" style="s2">thought someone in your position would marry <br />a socialite, an aerys, not someone like me.</p>
<p begin="00:08:41.297" end="00:08:47.997" style="s2">Mr. Gray, I won&#39;t try to marry you again. Please <br />let me go. Don&#39;t throw me in. I won&#39;t do it again.</p>
<p begin="00:08:55.497" end="00:08:59.597" style="s2">Now you have no competition. You know <br />what to do, don&#39;t you, Mrs. Gray?</p>
<p begin="00:09:08.497" end="00:09:16.097" style="s2">This is every dollar I&#39;ve earned and spent for the <br />past few years. I used to show it to Simon. From  </p>
<p begin="00:09:16.097" end="00:09:23.797" style="s2">now on, I&#39;ll show it to you. I&#39;m your wife now. <br />I&#39;ll be completely faithful to you. I won&#39;t hide  </p>
<p begin="00:09:23.797" end="00:09:32.297" style="s2">anything. You think I need your money? We&#39;re in <br />this together. I need to pull my weight. I don&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="00:09:32.297" end="00:09:38.197" style="s2">make much now, but I&#39;ve been researching AI. <br />Once I get a patent, I&#39;ll be able to help you.</p>
<p begin="00:09:43.097" end="00:09:48.997" style="s2">As my wife, you get a million dollars a month <br />to spend. Your only job is to keep me happy.  </p>
<p begin="00:09:51.497" end="00:09:55.597" style="s2">A million a month. You want to pay <br />me to sit here and look pretty?  </p>
<p begin="00:09:56.497" end="00:10:01.897" style="s2">A wife, a kept woman. What does it matter? <br />As long as you&#39;re living well. [snorts]</p>
<p begin="00:10:04.597" end="00:10:08.397" style="s2">Game, what&#39;s a woman doing here? I <br />I have to get to work. I should go.  </p>
<p begin="00:10:09.697" end="00:10:13.498" style="s2">You never bring women here. Since when <br />did that change? She&#39;s your sister-in-law.  </p>
<p begin="00:10:14.098" end="00:10:21.098" style="s2">My sister-in-law. Blue Star <br />Golf Club. 100 p.m. Terrace 8.</p>
<p begin="00:10:24.298" end="00:10:30.598" style="s2">Blue Star. Isn&#39;t that the golf course you <br />started for fun back in college? What are  </p>
<p begin="00:10:30.598" end="00:10:36.698" style="s2">the odds? Looks like we were bound to cross <br />paths. [snorts] Come on, let&#39;s go take a look.</p>
<p begin="00:10:42.898" end="00:10:45.698" style="s2">Congratulations. What are you two doing here?  </p>
<p begin="00:10:46.298" end="00:10:51.698" style="s2">We&#39;re here to celebrate with you. Simon invited <br />us to celebrate the engagement. I can&#39;t believe  </p>
<p begin="00:10:51.698" end="00:10:56.898" style="s2">you&#39;re the first of us to get married. You <br />wouldn&#39;t even buy yourself decent clothes  </p>
<p begin="00:10:56.898" end="00:11:04.798" style="s2">because you were funding his business. It&#39;s <br />about time Simon proposed. [snorts] [music]  </p>
<p begin="00:11:04.798" end="00:11:07.998" style="s2">Why do you look like you sleep on the <br />street? Couldn&#39;t you wear something decent?  </p>
<p begin="00:11:09.198" end="00:11:11.898" style="s2">I don&#39;t mind wearing old clothes. We <br />can use the money to buy the models  </p>
<p begin="00:11:11.898" end="00:11:16.798" style="s2">you need. Someone did propose to <br />me today, but it wasn&#39;t Simon.  </p>
<p begin="00:11:17.698" end="00:11:21.698" style="s2">After everything you&#39;ve done for him, how could <br />he not propose? Why is that so hard to believe?</p>
<p begin="00:11:24.798" end="00:11:29.798" style="s2">Fiona, we&#39;re best friends. What&#39;s your <br />problem? I proposed to Fiona. She&#39;s my fianceé.  </p>
<p begin="00:11:30.398" end="00:11:34.398" style="s2">Simon, [snorts] what are you talking about? <br />Was I not clear? I&#39;m done with that loser,  </p>
<p begin="00:11:34.398" end="00:11:40.198" style="s2">Laya. Let me make it official. My fiance is <br />Fiona, the marketing manager at one of San  </p>
<p begin="00:11:40.198" end="00:11:45.998" style="s2">Francisco&#39;s leading tech companies. She makes over <br />$10,000 a month. Not this broke little nobody.  </p>
<p begin="00:11:46.698" end="00:11:49.398" style="s2">You were like a sister to me. <br />How could you steal my boyfriend?  </p>
<p begin="00:11:51.898" end="00:11:56.398" style="s2">Leela, I didn&#39;t make Simon dump you. You couldn&#39;t <br />keep your boyfriend interested. How is that my  </p>
<p begin="00:11:56.398" end="00:12:02.098" style="s2">fault? [music] Fiona, why are you wasting your <br />breath on some waitress at a golf club? She  </p>
<p begin="00:12:02.098" end="00:12:07.598" style="s2">makes next to nothing. She&#39;s beneath you. So, <br />you proposed to my best friend because I don&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="00:12:07.598" end="00:12:12.298" style="s2">make enough money. Of course, I want someone <br />who can help me get ahead. How&#39;s your lousy  </p>
<p begin="00:12:12.298" end="00:12:17.299" style="s2">paycheck supposed to fund my startup? Thank god <br />you never proposed to me. Marrying you would have  </p>
<p begin="00:12:17.300" end="00:12:21.300" style="s2">been the biggest mistake of my life. [clears <br />throat] I hope you two stay together forever.  </p>
<p begin="00:12:21.900" end="00:12:26.900" style="s2">Maybe that&#39;ll keep you from wrecking anyone else&#39;s <br />relationship. Simon, what the hell are you doing?  </p>
<p begin="00:12:28.700" end="00:12:33.300" style="s2">Simon, just because I used to love you doesn&#39;t <br />mean you get to treat me like this. Remember,  </p>
<p begin="00:12:33.300" end="00:12:38.100" style="s2">we&#39;re paying customers. We can treat you however <br />we want. As far as I&#39;m concerned, you&#39;re trash.  </p>
<p begin="00:12:38.100" end="00:12:43.300" style="s2">Fiona, you stole Yla&#39;s husband. And now <br />you&#39;re saying this, have you no shame?  </p>
<p begin="00:12:43.300" end="00:12:48.800" style="s2">Fiona, making a million a year doesn&#39;t make <br />you special. Laya was a top student at MIT.  </p>
<p begin="00:12:48.800" end="00:12:54.600" style="s2">She&#39;s going to go a lot further than you. A <br />loser who can&#39;t do anything but wait tables  </p>
<p begin="00:12:54.600" end="00:12:59.500" style="s2">is claiming she was a top student at MIT. How <br />embarrassing. What&#39;s all this shouting about?  </p>
<p begin="00:13:02.100" end="00:13:05.600" style="s2">They&#39;re harassing one of your employees. <br />You&#39;re the manager. You need to do something.  </p>
<p begin="00:13:07.700" end="00:13:11.400" style="s2">Who said you could insult our <br />guests? Apologize to them now. Fiona,  </p>
<p begin="00:13:11.400" end="00:13:15.100" style="s2">we&#39;re honored you chose to visit our <br />club. I wouldn&#39;t normally come here,  </p>
<p begin="00:13:15.100" end="00:13:20.000" style="s2">but one of your waitresses had the nerve to <br />hit on my mail. She needs to pay for that.  </p>
<p begin="00:13:20.700" end="00:13:25.700" style="s2">Who would dare do something like that? <br />Leela, the one who stalks your cigars. Fiona,  </p>
<p begin="00:13:25.700" end="00:13:30.400" style="s2">I&#39;ll make sure that loser learns her lesson. Just <br />put in a good word for me with Mr. Gray, will you?  </p>
<p begin="00:13:30.400" end="00:13:35.600" style="s2">Don&#39;t worry. Handle this properly and I&#39;ll make it <br />worth your while. Are you deaf? Apologize to us.  </p>
<p begin="00:13:38.300" end="00:13:42.300" style="s2">They&#39;re the ones in the wrong. Why should I <br />apologize? What did you just say? The customer  </p>
<p begin="00:13:42.300" end="00:13:46.700" style="s2">is always right at marketing. Do you really <br />think you can afford to cross her, Mr. Gray?</p>
<p begin="00:13:49.500" end="00:13:55.300" style="s2">Excuse me. You dropped your bread. I found this <br />lucky coin by the fountain this morning. I&#39;d like  </p>
<p begin="00:13:55.300" end="00:14:00.200" style="s2">you to have it. I hope it brings you good luck. <br />She&#39;s really something. Gayen, what is it about  </p>
<p begin="00:14:00.200" end="00:14:05.500" style="s2">Yla? What&#39;s got you so hooked? You&#39;ll see what <br />I mean when you meet her. Leela&#39;s friends will  </p>
<p begin="00:14:05.500" end="00:14:10.200" style="s2">be there, too. Is everything arranged? Relax. <br />I&#39;ve got it covered. We&#39;ll make sure gets the  </p>
<p begin="00:14:10.200" end="00:14:16.001" style="s2">VIP treatment. Leela, why are you just standing <br />there? Mr. Gray runs the largest tech company in  </p>
<p begin="00:14:16.001" end="00:14:20.101" style="s2">San Francisco. He&#39;s one of the richest men <br />in Silicon Valley. Everyone respects him.  </p>
<p begin="00:14:20.701" end="00:14:24.201" style="s2">I don&#39;t know how powerful Mr. Gray is, but I <br />know a man like him would care who&#39;s right and  </p>
<p begin="00:14:24.201" end="00:14:27.701" style="s2">who&#39;s wrong. He wouldn&#39;t let you bully people <br />like this. What are you going to tell us?  </p>
<p begin="00:14:27.701" end="00:14:32.301" style="s2">Mr. Gray was the one who proposed to you today. <br />Wouldn&#39;t be part of his world. Stop bullying her.  </p>
<p begin="00:14:32.301" end="00:14:37.701" style="s2">Am I wrong? She needs a reality check. All she <br />wants is a rich man to latch on to. I invited  </p>
<p begin="00:14:37.701" end="00:14:42.001" style="s2">you here so you&#39;d see what Leela really is. <br />Even I don&#39;t want her. Why would Mr. Gray  </p>
<p begin="00:14:42.001" end="00:14:48.301" style="s2">marry her? Leela, a gentleman who says he&#39;s your <br />husband ordered this box of lady cigars for you.  </p>
<p begin="00:14:48.901" end="00:14:54.301" style="s2">My husband? Those are David Oas. <br />Aren&#39;t those really expensive?  </p>
<p begin="00:14:54.901" end="00:14:59.101" style="s2">How could someone as broke as Yla afford <br />cigars like that? They have to be fake.  </p>
<p begin="00:15:01.201" end="00:15:06.301" style="s2">They&#39;re real Davids. Wow. Yla&#39;s got some serious <br />money if [snorts] she finds cigars like these.  </p>
